• Treat the circles as a single “stack” and optionally shift that stack upward  
• Let the top-of-green oval sit level with the bottom-of-purple circle  
• Right-align (and slightly shorten) the yellow bar, give it a blue outline, and nudge it closer to the top

Because our grammar has no grouping or CSS, the best we can do is hard-code those results by changing:  
– stroke_color to “none” (and stroke_width 0) on the purple, blue and orange circles  
– y (and sometimes x / size) values to move blocks as a whole  
– rectangle x / scale_x / y / stroke_color to match the new anchoring

Below are five different takes, ranging from a light touch (Candidate 1) to more aggressive re-spacing and re-sizing (Candidate 3).  Candidates 4 & 5 experiment with slightly different offsets and x-positions to give diversity.
